    gui_retained_render_session_cpu_seed_preflight_rejected_2026-11-13, P3, fixed, "GuiRetainedRenderSession.seed rejected on cpu backend: fresh-device-command-preflight-required", doc/08_tracking/bug/gui_retained_render_session_cpu_seed_preflight_rejected_2026-11-13.md, 1, test/01_unit/lib/gc_async_mut/ui/gui_content_renderer_spec.spl, 2026-11-13, 2026-11-13, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    gui_retained_render_session_cpu_seed_preflight_rejected_2026-11-13, 0, "2026-11-13: release/1.0.0 35144b7f5e9, Linux aarch64 seed af717f53d6bce3e5: gui_content_renderer_spec.spl 3 examples, 2 failures; probe of engine2d_draw_ir_render_composition_damaged_with_images on a column+label tree 32x16 cpu -> unsupported=fresh-device-command-preflight-required ops=0 src=preflight_rejected. Refused command and introducing commit not established."
    gui_retained_render_session_cpu_seed_preflight_rejected_2026-11-13, 1, "2026-11-13: refused command identified: label text command at x=3 width=36 on a 32-wide full-target batch; fresh-device preflight is called with allow_clipped=false and rejects text that is not wholly bounded (draw_ir_adv.spl:1210). Open question: text-metric drift vs intended clipped-text admission."

    gui_retained_render_session_cpu_seed_preflight_rejected_2026-11-13, 2, "2026-11-13 lane uia2: FIXED. Not metric drift: the label overhung the 32px fixture when the spec landed (9dc4e88f661) and passed because seed used the ordered composition executor. d86b7ef59e2 moved seed to the tiled damage wrapper whose fresh-device preflight rejects it; relaxing that preflight only exposes retained-composition-unsafe-embedding (default theme root samples its parent). Fix: seed uses engine2d_draw_ir_adv_composition_owner_with_images. gui_content_renderer_spec red 5 examples 3 failures (f06707aaef0) then 5 examples 0 failures on release/1.0.0 d66bc5eaf82. Remaining: a non-idle damage plan is still rejected with retained-composition-unsafe-embedding; see the document."
